      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_68",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/frontier.webp"),
            text: _("24 Deeproot, 501 YW The sun don’t really shine at all in these Grey Woods, but truth be told, I has been getting used to it more and more. Lounging out in the warm daylight, talkin’ with Erwen while watching them kids play out in the fields... those times were so long ago. Our lives weren’t never real peaceful, but back then, we had our homes and our friends and our family... now we be creatures of the dark."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_69",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/frontier.webp"),
            text: _("It be real lonesome like this. I still has me Harper, and I be grateful for the lass, but she don’t really understand an old man like me. I know the past be the past, but I just can’t help but think of sis in times like these. How she used to be dragging me out on some silly little romp, a little job here and there for some gold or lil trinket, or sometimes just for fun... I never wanted to go, of course. I were always real lazy. Still am, even now."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_70",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/frontier.webp"),
            text: _("Then, Harper tells me, “Come on Uncle, we’re on an adventure! Don’t be so mopey, live a little!” I know she be trying to be cheery, but she really don’t know how much she be reminding me of Erwen sometimes..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_71",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/frontier.webp"),
            text: _("I must be strong. That’s what I tells myself. I should be strong, but... I don’t know what be keeping me going, if it be this misguided sense of pride, or my duties to the village, or Harper, or even just remembering the past, making some futile attempts to go back to better times."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_72",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/frontier.webp"),
            text: _("Either way, I be here now, on this adventure."),
          },
        ],
      },
